For a video request, use a video URL that the server can access. The example below uses a public sample video; for local files, mount the host media directory to `/media` and use a `file:///media/...` URL instead:

```bash
curl http://<server_ip>:<port>/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "model": "qwen3-vl-30b",
    "messages": [
      {"role": "user", "content": [
        {"type": "video_url", "video_url": {"url": "https://qianwen-res.oss-cn-beijing.aliyuncs.com/Qwen3-Omni/demo/draw.mp4"}},
        {"type": "text", "text": "Describe this video."}
      ]}
    ],
    "max_completion_tokens": 256,
    "temperature": 0
  }'
```

